ASTC IsOpaque reads each block header with one load and a table of the 2048 block modes.
(ProsperoEden eglantine-a42b4d4-ps5.d 0045 astc-opaque-scan-table.)

IsOpaque (the BC1-or-BC3 choice for each new ASTC texture, a scan of every block on the GPU thread)
decoded each block's header bit by bit, apart from EglantinePS5's single-partition shortcut. Every
block now takes the table (what DecodeBlockInfo makes of each 11-bit mode), multi-partition and
void-extent blocks included: same result on 20M random blocks, 5.5x faster in ProsperoEden (42 ->
8 ms for 16 MiB); here checked against the bit-by-bit decode on 4M random blocks.
EDEN_NX2_ASTC_OPAQUE_SLOW=1 still decodes every block.

